Italdesign is an Italian design and engineering company specializing in automotive, transportation, and product development sectors. Based in Moncalieri (Turin) with over 1,300 employees worldwide, it has been shaping innovation and collaborating with leading car manufacturers and emerging players for more than 55 years.


Renowned for its pivotal role in automotive design, Italdesign has developed iconic vehicles and offers comprehensive services spanning exterior and interior design, prototyping, engineering, and turnkey project management. Its vertical integrated approach ensures seamless support throughout the product lifecycle, from initial concept to homologation and series production, delivering solutions tailored to client needs.


As an incubator of innovative technologies, Italdesign fosters advancements in mobility and prototyping. In recent years, it has expanded into electronic systems development, including infotainment, ADAS, high\\-voltage batteries, and Software Defined Vehicles (SDVs). This blend of technical expertise and creative design solidifies its position as a reference point in the industry.


Since joining the Audi Group in 2010, Italdesign has continued to grow, combining aesthetics and functionality to pioneer cutting\\-edge solutions that meet the demands of a rapidly evolving market. In 2024 Italdesign obtained the Top Employers Certification for the ninth consecutive year.





**Posizione:**
--------------

Italdesign is looking for enthusiastic graduating and new graduated engineers passionate about automotive willing to join an innovative and international business environment, working in an agile way and enjoying the teamwork spirit.


You will gain a great experience learning all the instruments, procedures, and technical aspects with the support of colleagues of the Department.


According to your interests and educational background, you will develop skills within some different areas related to Electric and Electronic field:

* UX/UI
* Software development
* Connectivity (protocols and technologies, development of connected features))
* System platform and functions (operating systems, embedded systems and feature development)

**Requisiti:**
--------------

**Key requirements**

* Master's degree students or master's degree new graduates less than 2 years ago;
* Eligible to work full\\-time in Italy;
* Good knowledge of Microsoft Office Package (Word, Excel, PowerPoint);
* Passion and interest in Automotive Sector and in Electric/Electronic sector;
* Good team working skills;
* Good interpersonal and communicative skills;
* Good time management capability and proactivity;
* Ability to manage problems and propose solutions.

 **Preferential requirements**

* Knowledge of the automotive domain;
* Knowledge of processes and contents related to at least one of the following domains: Human\\-Machine Interaction Development / Components Development / Infotainment Development / Connectivity Development / Software Development;
* Knowledge of requirements management;
* Knowledge or short Experience in Object\\-Oriented Programming (Java or C\\+\\+);
* Knowledge or short Experience with both Waterfall and Agile Scrum methodologies;
* Understanding of vehicle level system integration in terms of hardware and software.

**Altre informazioni:**
-----------------------

**Education:** Master’s degree in engineering (Telecommunication and Digital Media, Electronics, Computer, Automation and Robotics, Transportation and Mobility, Autonomous Vehicle, Data Science)

**Language skills:** Fluent knowledge of written and spoken English (at least B2 level); Excellent knowledge of written and spoken Italian; basic German would be appreciated (with willingness to improve).

**Workplace:** Naples, Italy.

**Benefit:** continuous training (technical, soft and languages skills), good work\\-life balance, multicultural environment.

 *Italdesign is committed to create an inclusive, diverse and safe workplace,*

*and we are proud to be an equal opportunity employer (L.903/77\\). We welcome applications from all candidates, regardless of the gender, ethnic, religion, sexual orientation, disability, parental status, or social origin.*

