TXT Group is an international end\\-to\\-end IT consulting provider of software solutions and services, supporting the digital transformation of clients' core products and processes. With a proprietary software portfolio and deep expertise in vertical domains, TXT Group operates in diverse markets, with a growing footprint in the aerospace, aviation, defense, industrial, government, and fintech sectors. The parent company TXT e\\-solutions S.p.A. has been listed on the Italian Stock Exchange, on the Star Segment (TXT.MI), since July 2000\\. TXT Group is headquartered in Milan and has subsidiaries in Italy, Germany, the United Kingdom, France, Switzerland and the United States of America.



**System Engineer \\- Fuel System:**  

TXT e\\-Tech, for its Aerospace\\&Aviation division, is looking for a System Engineer specialised in Fuel systems who will be in charge of requirements definition, physical and functional modelling and support to the equipment engineer.



The selected resource will work within a multidisciplinary team and will be involved in the different phases of the system life cycle, from the definition of the architecture to technical validation with suppliers.



**Main responsibilities:**  

**System Requirements \\& Architecture Definition:**  

Analysis of L1 (aircraft) requirements and derivation of L2 requirements at system and Fuel subsystem level;

Analysis of airworthiness requirements applicable to the Fuel system;

Definition of system requirements, including fuel centre of gravity (CG) management;

Support for preliminary Fuel system architecture definition.



**Physical modelling of the system:**  

Development of physical simulation models of the Fuel subsystems (e.g. sloshing, CG, pressure drops, tank\\-to\\-tank transfers);

Analysis for functional and performance dimensioning of subsystems;

Cyclic updating of models based on information from suppliers;



**Functional modelling:**  

Development of functional models of the Fuel system;

Definition of interfaces, use cases and validation of the architecture in different operating scenarios;

Support in defining and allocating detailed requirements;

Model Based System Engineering (MBSE).



**Equipment engineering:**  

Drafting of preliminary supply specifications;

Technical analysis of supplier proposals;

Participation in the document update process and conducting KoM and design reviews.



**Technical skills required:**  

Expertise in systems engineering and aeronautics;

Knowledge of design processes in aeronautics;

Ability to develop simulation models of concentrated\\-parameter and one\\-dimensional environmental control systems and knowledge of systems simulation tools (Simcenter Amesim, MATLAB/Simulink);

Knowledge of fluid dynamic simulation and 3D design tools (StarCCM\\+ and Catia V5\\);

Good knowledge of spoken and written English



**Optional technical skills:**  

Familiarity with technical documents, standards and aviation regulations;

Knowledge of requirements management methods and related tools (DOORS);

Ability to develop functional modelling of a system with the use of related tools (preferably CAMEO);

Expertise in the fuel system and related components (pumps, valves, etc.)



**Why choose TXT Group:**  

Career opportunity in a fast\\-growing company;

Opportunity to work in an international, young and dynamic environment;

Corporate Benefits (health insurance, welfare, Ticket Restaurant, discounts as a group employee);

